# No co-authors in commits

When creating git commits in this repository:

- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by:` (or any co-author trailer) to the commit message
- Do **not** attribute Cursor, Claude, or other AI tools as co-authors
- Commit messages should contain only the subject/body describing the change

```bash
# ❌ BAD
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Add auth module.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
EOF
)"

# ✅ GOOD
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Add auth module.

EOF
)"
```
